{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And behold, they were downcast.</b> The reason for the downcast faces of both of them, according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Berakhot 55b), is that each one dreamed also the interpretation of the other's dream. Therefore the chief butler was troubled by what he saw in the other's interpretation, for it was bad, and he was afraid for himself as well and alarmed; and the chief baker — even though he dreamed the other's interpretation for good, despite all this, being subject to misfortune, his star foretold him and his heart was not settled with him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:09.500820233Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}